course: dictionary
lesson: 4128
title: Glide: smooth movement and gliding flight
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To glide is to move smoothly and quietly, without effort, as if sliding. «A swan glides across the still lake.» The swan does not flap or jump. It moves calmly and easily, and that is what glide means.
explain: Glide can also describe flight. «Birds like eagles and albatrosses glide on air currents, slowly losing height.» A paper plane does the same: it flies through the air without flapping wings or using an engine.
explain: Glide can be a noun too, meaning a smooth, sliding movement. Use the context to decide which meaning fits. If the sentence is about a bird, a plane or a skater, the words around glide will show you which one the writer means.
fact: To glide means to move smoothly and quietly, as if sliding.
fact: For a bird or plane, to glide means to fly without flapping wings or using an engine.
fact: A glide is a smooth, sliding movement.
fact: «A sugar glider glides from tree to tree» using a skin flap between its front and back legs.
fact: Gliding shows how air can hold up wings, so gliders and paper planes stay in the air for a while.
exercise: «The swan glided across the still lake.» What does glided mean here? | Made a loud splash | Sank under the water | Flapped its wings very fast | *Moved smoothly and quietly
exercise: «The albatross glided on the air currents for hours.» What does glide mean here? | *Flew without flapping its wings | Sang loudly | Dived straight into the sea | Ran across the sand
exercise: «The skater's glide across the ice looked effortless.» What kind of word is glide in this sentence? | Verb | *Noun | Adjective | Adverb
test: «The ghost glided through the wall without a sound.» What does glided suggest? | *Moved smoothly and silently | Jumped high into the air | Crashed into the wall | Walked very loudly
test: «The paper plane glided slowly down the hall.» Which meaning of glide fits here? | To stamp loudly on the floor | To fall asleep in a chair | *To fly without an engine, slowly down
exam: Which sentence uses glide as a noun? | «The skaters glided past the crowd.» | «She glides like a dancer.» | «The skater will glide across the ice.» | *«The skater's glide was smooth and perfect.»
